<article class="env-definition" id="01HK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01HK">Definition <span data-tag="01HK">26.4.1</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a morphism of locally ringed spaces. We say that $i$ is a <em>closed immersion</em> if: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The map $i$ is a homeomorphism of $Z$ onto a closed subset of $X$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The map $\mathcal{O}_ X \to i_*\mathcal{O}_ Z$ is surjective; let $\mathcal{I}$ denote the kernel. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{I}$ is locally generated by sections. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>